  "_comment": [
    "Bilingual search lexicon. Each group is one concept; every surface in the",
    "group is treated as equivalent at query time, so typing any of them finds",
    "content spelled with any other — including across scripts, which is what",
    "makes an English query reach a Hebrew-titled shiur.",
    "",
    "Surfaces are folded through search.fold1() on insert, so they use the exact",
    "same normalisation as the corpus. Do NOT pre-fold entries here; write them",
    "the way a person would type them.",
    "",
    "Only spellings the conservative fold and skeleton do NOT already merge need",
    "listing. basra/batra already collapse to 'bsr' automatically; the value here",
    "is the Hebrew<->Latin link and the irregular forms.",
    "",
    "Add entries freely — this is applied at QUERY time, so edits take effect",
    "immediately with no re-backfill of the 1.65M-row episodes table."
  ],

